1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:04,420
A response vehicle drives out of coverage. The
network changes.

2
00:00:04,420 --> 00:00:06,300
The session should not have to.

3
00:00:06,800 --> 00:00:12,500
Everything here is a software simulation. No
radios, no satellite, no hardware.

4
00:00:12,900 --> 00:00:15,528
The reactive baseline waits for its link to
fail.

5
00:00:15,528 --> 00:00:20,300
Here the session goes dark four times: seven
point three two seconds, one full reconnect.

6
00:00:20,800 --> 00:00:24,153
CONTINUA is the working application around
that problem.

7
00:00:24,153 --> 00:00:26,847
Every panel reads from one engine over a live

8
00:00:26,847 --> 00:00:29,900
socket, and the execution mode is always on
screen.

9
00:00:30,300 --> 00:00:33,203
Five steps. Observe: receiver side facts only.

10
00:00:33,203 --> 00:00:36,800
The controller never sees the script the world
runs from.

11
00:00:37,200 --> 00:00:41,600
Predict: a short horizon on those same facts,
three seconds ahead.

12
00:00:41,900 --> 00:00:44,403
Prepare: at twenty eight point eight seconds
it

13
00:00:44,403 --> 00:00:46,800
warms cellular while Wi-Fi is still carrying.

14
00:00:46,900 --> 00:00:52,400
Steer, six tenths of a second later. Explain:
it records why, as it decided.

15
00:00:52,600 --> 00:00:55,233
Same seed, same trace, only the policy
changed.

16
00:00:55,233 --> 00:00:58,483
Seven point three two seconds of interruption
becomes zero

17
00:00:58,483 --> 00:01:01,900
point one six, and that remainder is the
session starting up.

18
00:01:02,600 --> 00:01:07,140
On the satellite route it holds the session
through the fallback, and spends

19
00:01:07,140 --> 00:01:11,800
four point eight megabytes of satellite where
the baseline spends forty seven.

20
00:01:12,600 --> 00:01:16,038
Twenty paired trials say something we did not
expect.

21
00:01:16,038 --> 00:01:18,957
Preparation is what removes the interruption.

22
00:01:18,957 --> 00:01:22,200
Take the predictor out and almost nothing
changes.

23
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:26,640
What CONTINUA adds is the price: the same
continuity at

24
00:01:26,640 --> 00:01:30,148
a third of the cost, a twelfth of the
satellite data.

25
00:01:30,148 --> 00:01:32,200
It loses on application health.

26
00:01:32,600 --> 00:01:34,979
Scope. A simulation, not a network.

27
00:01:34,979 --> 00:01:38,854
Emulation is unverified here and the kernel
has no MPTCP.

28
00:01:38,854 --> 00:01:43,000
When every link is down: ten point six
seconds, every policy.

29
00:01:43,600 --> 00:01:48,600
CONTINUA. Predictive network continuity. By
Team Kanban.
